{"instance_id": "households_1", "selected_database": "households", "audit_status": "unrecoverable", "original_sol_sql": ["WITH ComfortIndex AS (SELECT h.locregion, AVG(CAST(REPLACE(JSON_EXTRACT(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Bath_Count'), '\"', '') AS REAL) / NULLIF(h.residentcount, 0)) AS avg_comfort FROM households h JOIN properties p ON h.housenum = p.houselink WHERE JSON_EXTRACT(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Bath_Count') IS NOT NULL GROUP BY h.locregion), TopRegion AS (SELECT locregion FROM ComfortIndex ORDER BY avg_comfort DESC LIMIT 1) SELECT SUM(CAST(REPLACE(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Auto_Count'), '\"', '') AS INTEGER)) FROM transportation_assets t JOIN households h ON t.housetag = h.housenum WHERE h.locregion = (SELECT locregion FROM TopRegion);"], "audited_sol_sql": ["SELECT h.locregion AS area_code, AVG(CAST(REPLACE(JSON_EXTRACT(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Bath_Count'), '\"', '') AS REAL) / NULLIF(h.residentcount, 0)) AS avg_bathroom_ratio FROM households h JOIN properties p ON h.housenum = p.houselink WHERE JSON_EXTRACT(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Bath_Count') IS NOT NULL GROUP BY h.locregion;"], "audited_sample_row": [" CEIL\u00c2NDIA", 0.3333333333333333], "changes": [{"clause_kind": "outer_select", "original": "SELECT SUM(... Auto_Count ...) FROM transportation_assets WHERE locregion = (TopRegion of avg bathroom ratio)", "replacement": "SELECT h.locregion AS area_code, AVG(bath_count / residents) AS avg_bathroom_ratio FROM households JOIN properties ... GROUP BY h.locregion", "why_unjustified": "The user asked for area_code + average bathroom ratio per area; the gold returns a single SUM of car counts for the top-bathroom-ratio region. Neither the join to transportation_assets nor the SUM(Auto_Count) projection is justified by any KB entry, column-meaning, or labeled-ambiguity. The user query contains no reference to vehicles.", "justified_by": ["labeled_ambiguity:typical bathroom ratio", "labeled_ambiguity:area code", "knowledge_ambiguity:Bathroom Ratio", "kb:15", "primitive"]}], "reasoning_summary": "The gold's intent doesn't match the user's question: it returns a single SUM of car counts (Auto_Count) for the top-region, while the user asked for area + avg bathroom ratio per area. The bathroom-ratio CTE in the gold is correctly defined (matching labeled_ambiguity 'typical bathroom ratio' + KB 15), so we replace the entire query with that CTE materialised as the SELECT, grouped by area.", "skill_version": "audit-gold-sql/1.0", "audited_at": "2026-05-14T11:47:11+00:00"}
{"instance_id": "households_2", "selected_database": "households", "audit_status": "clean", "original_sol_sql": ["WITH HighRisk AS (SELECT h.housenum, h.locregion FROM households h JOIN service_types s ON h.serviceplan = s.serviceref JOIN transportation_assets t ON h.housenum = t.housetag WHERE s.socsupport = 'Yes' AND (CAST(json_extract(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Auto_Count') AS INTEGER) + CAST(json_extract(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Bike_Count') AS INTEGER) + CAST(json_extract(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Motor_Count') AS INTEGER)) > 2 AND (json_extract(t.vehicleinventory, '$.Newest_Year') IN ('2010 to 2013', '2012 To 2013', '2014 or newer'))), RegionalCounts AS (SELECT locregion, COUNT(*) AS high_risk_count FROM HighRisk GROUP BY locregion), TotalCounts AS (SELECT locregion, COUNT(*) AS total_count FROM households GROUP BY locregion) SELECT rc.locregion FROM RegionalCounts rc JOIN TotalCounts tc ON rc.locregion = tc.locregion ORDER BY (CAST(rc.high_risk_count AS REAL) / tc.total_count) DESC LIMIT 1;"], "audited_sol_sql": ["WITH HighRisk AS (SELECT h.housenum, h.locregion FROM households h JOIN service_types s ON h.serviceplan = s.serviceref JOIN transportation_assets t ON h.housenum = t.housetag WHERE s.socsupport = 'Yes' AND (CAST(json_extract(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Auto_Count') AS INTEGER) + CAST(json_extract(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Bike_Count') AS INTEGER) + CAST(json_extract(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Motor_Count') AS INTEGER)) > 2 AND (json_extract(t.vehicleinventory, '$.Newest_Year') IN ('2010 to 2013', '2012 To 2013', '2014 or newer'))), RegionalCounts AS (SELECT locregion, COUNT(*) AS high_risk_count FROM HighRisk GROUP BY locregion), TotalCounts AS (SELECT locregion, COUNT(*) AS total_count FROM households GROUP BY locregion) SELECT rc.locregion FROM RegionalCounts rc JOIN TotalCounts tc ON rc.locregion = tc.locregion ORDER BY (CAST(rc.high_risk_count AS REAL) / tc.total_count) DESC LIMIT 1;"], "audited_sample_row": ["Riacho  Fundo I"], "changes": [], "reasoning_summary": "Every clause is justified. 'High-risk families' = supported AND mobile is fully covered by labeled_ambiguity 'high-risk families' (which encodes socsupport='Yes' + vehicles>2 + recent-year-list). 'highest concentration' = ratio-sort + LIMIT 1 is labeled. 'Where' = locregion projection is labeled. KB 23 (Mobile Household) + KB 24 (Supported Household) + KB 9 + KB 10 + KB 14 cover the per-leg semantics. The dataset's choice to define 'high-risk' as 'supported AND mobile' is unusual but is the dataset's sanctioned definition (labeled_ambiguity is the canonical authority).", "skill_version": "audit-gold-sql/1.0", "audited_at": "2026-05-14T11:47:11+00:00"}
{"instance_id": "households_3", "selected_database": "households", "audit_status": "clean", "original_sol_sql": ["SELECT DISTINCT h.housenum FROM households h JOIN service_types s ON h.serviceplan = s.serviceref JOIN transportation_assets t ON h.housenum = t.housetag WHERE s.socsupport = 'Yes' AND (COALESCE(CAST(json_extract(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Auto_Count') AS INTEGER), 0) + COALESCE(CAST(json_extract(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Bike_Count') AS INTEGER), 0) + COALESCE(CAST(json_extract(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Motor_Count') AS INTEGER), 0)) > 2 AND (json_extract(t.vehicleinventory, '$.Newest_Year') IN ('2010 to 2013', '2012 To 2013', '2014 or newer'));"], "audited_sol_sql": ["SELECT DISTINCT h.housenum FROM households h JOIN service_types s ON h.serviceplan = s.serviceref JOIN transportation_assets t ON h.housenum = t.housetag WHERE s.socsupport = 'Yes' AND (COALESCE(CAST(json_extract(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Auto_Count') AS INTEGER), 0) + COALESCE(CAST(json_extract(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Bike_Count') AS INTEGER), 0) + COALESCE(CAST(json_extract(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Motor_Count') AS INTEGER), 0)) > 2 AND (json_extract(t.vehicleinventory, '$.Newest_Year') IN ('2010 to 2013', '2012 To 2013', '2014 or newer'));"], "audited_sample_row": [348], "changes": [], "reasoning_summary": "Every clause is justified. 'receiving aid' = socsupport='Yes' is labeled. 'have a lot of vehicles' is labeled as full Mobile-Household predicate (vehicles>2 + year-in-list), also covered by knowledge_ambiguity 'Mobile Household' (deleted_kb=23). DISTINCT housenum matches the user's request for 'IDs'. The dataset bundles 'a lot of vehicles' with the recent-year condition, which is unusual but is the labeled-ambiguity's sanctioned meaning.", "skill_version": "audit-gold-sql/1.0", "audited_at": "2026-05-14T11:47:11+00:00"}
{"instance_id": "households_4", "selected_database": "households", "audit_status": "clean", "original_sol_sql": ["SELECT COUNT(*) FROM (SELECT ((COALESCE(CAST(json_extract(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Bath_Count') AS REAL), 0) * 10 + COALESCE(CAST(json_extract(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Room_Count') AS REAL), 0) * 15) / NULLIF(h.residentcount, 0)) AS sq_meters_per_resident FROM properties AS p JOIN households AS h ON p.houselink = h.housenum WHERE LOWER(json_extract(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Dwelling_Class')) = 'apartment') AS space_details WHERE sq_meters_per_resident > 20;"], "audited_sol_sql": ["SELECT COUNT(*) FROM (SELECT ((COALESCE(CAST(json_extract(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Bath_Count') AS REAL), 0) * 10 + COALESCE(CAST(json_extract(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Room_Count') AS REAL), 0) * 15) / NULLIF(h.residentcount, 0)) AS sq_meters_per_resident FROM properties AS p JOIN households AS h ON p.houselink = h.housenum WHERE LOWER(json_extract(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Dwelling_Class')) = 'apartment') AS space_details WHERE sq_meters_per_resident > 20;"], "audited_sample_row": [86], "changes": [], "reasoning_summary": "Every clause is justified. 'apartment' = Dwelling_Class='apartment' is labeled. 'square meters per resident' = (bath*10 + room*15)/residents is labeled, including the 10/15 multipliers and the > 20 threshold (Space Bonus). knowledge_ambiguity 'Space Bonus' (deleted_kb=29) corroborates. COUNT(*) over the subquery is primitive. KB 17 (Dwelling Capacity) and KB 29 (Comfortable Living Household) provide the conceptual scaffolding.", "skill_version": "audit-gold-sql/1.0", "audited_at": "2026-05-14T11:47:11+00:00"}
{"instance_id": "households_5", "selected_database": "households", "audit_status": "unrecoverable", "original_sol_sql": ["WITH AffluentLarge AS (SELECT h.housenum, h.locregion, h.loczone FROM households h WHERE (json_extract(h.socioeconomic, '$.Income_Bracket') IN ('More than R$ 4,400', 'More than R$ 2,640 and less than R$ 4,400')) AND (UPPER(json_extract(h.socioeconomic, '$.Tenure_Type')) = 'OWNED') AND h.residentcount > 4) SELECT locregion, CAST(loczone AS INTEGER) FROM AffluentLarge ORDER BY housenum ASC LIMIT 1;"], "audited_sol_sql": ["SELECT h.housenum, h.locregion, h.loczone, h.residentcount FROM households h WHERE (json_extract(h.socioeconomic, '$.Income_Bracket') IN ('More than R$ 4,400', 'More than R$ 2,640 and less than R$ 4,400')) AND (UPPER(json_extract(h.socioeconomic, '$.Tenure_Type')) = 'OWNED') ORDER BY h.residentcount DESC;"], "audited_sample_row": [803, "Samambaia", 353, 8], "changes": [{"clause_kind": "where_predicate", "original": "h.residentcount > 4", "replacement": "(removed)", "why_unjustified": "The threshold '4' for residentcount is not in any KB entry, column-meaning, or labeled-ambiguity sql_snippet. The labeled ambiguity for 'largest households' is 'ORDER BY h.residentcount DESC' \u2014 a ranking, not a threshold filter.", "justified_by": ["labeled_ambiguity:largest households"]}, {"clause_kind": "outer_select", "original": "SELECT locregion, CAST(loczone AS INTEGER) FROM AffluentLarge ORDER BY housenum ASC LIMIT 1", "replacement": "SELECT h.housenum, h.locregion, h.loczone, h.residentcount FROM households h WHERE ... ORDER BY h.residentcount DESC", "why_unjustified": "User asked for 'a list of households'; gold returns one row (LIMIT 1) with only locregion+loczone (drops housenum). ORDER BY housenum ASC isn't justified ('largest' labeled-ambiguity orders by residentcount DESC). Output shape and ordering both contradict the user query.", "justified_by": ["labeled_ambiguity:well-off", "labeled_ambiguity:largest households", "knowledge_ambiguity:Affluent Household", "kb:21", "primitive"]}], "reasoning_summary": "Gold filters by an unjustified residentcount > 4 threshold, drops housenum from the projection, sorts by housenum (not by 'largest'), and LIMITs to 1 row \u2014 all contradicting the user's request for 'a list' of households sorted by size. Audited SQL keeps the labeled 'well-off' predicate (Income_Bracket in the two highest brackets + Tenure='OWNED', class-3 + KB 21 justified), drops the threshold, restores housenum in the projection, and sorts by residentcount DESC per the labeled 'largest households' interpretation.", "skill_version": "audit-gold-sql/1.0", "audited_at": "2026-05-14T11:47:11+00:00"}
{"instance_id": "households_6", "selected_database": "households", "audit_status": "unrecoverable", "original_sol_sql": ["WITH Overcrowded AS (SELECT h.housenum FROM households h JOIN properties p ON h.housenum = p.houselink WHERE LOWER(h.locregion) = 'taguatinga' AND CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Room_Count') AS REAL) > 0 AND (h.residentcount / CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Room_Count') AS REAL)) > 3) SELECT ROUND(AVG(COALESCE(CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Auto_Count') AS INTEGER), 0) + COALESCE(CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Bike_Count') AS INTEGER), 0) + COALESCE(CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Motor_Count') AS INTEGER), 0))) FROM transportation_assets t JOIN Overcrowded o ON t.housetag = o.housenum;"], "audited_sol_sql": ["SELECT h.housenum, (h.residentcount / CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Room_Count') AS REAL)) AS density FROM households h JOIN properties p ON h.housenum = p.houselink WHERE LOWER(h.locregion) = 'taguatinga' AND CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Room_Count') AS REAL) > 0 ORDER BY density DESC;"], "audited_sample_row": [2336, 5.0], "changes": [{"clause_kind": "where_predicate", "original": "(h.residentcount / CAST(...$.Room_Count) > 3", "replacement": "(removed)", "why_unjustified": "The threshold '3' for density is not in any KB / column-meaning / labeled-ambiguity sql_snippet. The user did not ask to filter to overcrowded households \u2014 they asked for the density of *all* Taguatinga households with bedrooms.", "justified_by": ["labeled_ambiguity:Taguatinga area", "labeled_ambiguity:crowding metric"]}, {"clause_kind": "outer_select", "original": "SELECT ROUND(AVG(vehicle counts)) FROM transportation_assets t JOIN Overcrowded o ON ...", "replacement": "SELECT h.housenum, density FROM households h JOIN properties p WHERE ... ORDER BY density DESC", "why_unjustified": "User asked for (housenum, density) per Taguatinga household, sorted by density DESC. Gold returns a single number = average vehicle count among overcrowded Taguatinga households. The join to transportation_assets and the vehicle-count aggregation are unjustified by any source.", "justified_by": ["labeled_ambiguity:Taguatinga area", "labeled_ambiguity:crowding metric", "labeled_ambiguity:some bedrooms", "knowledge_ambiguity:Household Density", "kb:11", "primitive"]}], "reasoning_summary": "Gold returns a single SUM over a vehicle-count aggregation on 'overcrowded' households (density>3 threshold not in any source); user asked for a list of (household_id, crowding-metric) for all Taguatinga households with bedrooms, sorted by metric. Audited SQL implements exactly that natural reading using labeled-ambiguity-justified clauses for the area filter, density formula, and bedrooms guard.", "skill_version": "audit-gold-sql/1.0", "audited_at": "2026-05-14T11:47:11+00:00"}
{"instance_id": "households_7", "selected_database": "households", "audit_status": "edited", "original_sol_sql": ["WITH CrowdedStatus AS (SELECT CASE WHEN LOWER(i.wateraccess) IN ('yes', 'available at least in one room') AND LOWER(i.roadsurface) IN ('asphalt', 'concrete') THEN 'Urban' ELSE 'Rural' END AS location_type FROM households h JOIN properties p ON h.housenum = p.houselink JOIN infrastructure i ON p.infralink = i.infraref WHERE CAST(json_extract(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Room_Count') AS REAL) > 0 AND (h.residentcount / CAST(json_extract(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Room_Count') AS REAL)) > 2) SELECT COUNT(CASE WHEN location_type = 'Urban' THEN 1 END) - COUNT(CASE WHEN location_type = 'Rural' THEN 1 END) FROM CrowdedStatus;"], "audited_sol_sql": ["SELECT COUNT(*) FROM households h JOIN properties p ON h.housenum = p.houselink JOIN infrastructure i ON p.infralink = i.infraref WHERE CAST(json_extract(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Room_Count') AS REAL) > 0 AND (h.residentcount / CAST(json_extract(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Room_Count') AS REAL)) > 2 AND LOWER(i.wateraccess) IN ('yes', 'available at least in one room') AND LOWER(i.roadsurface) IN ('asphalt', 'concrete');"], "audited_sample_row": [0], "changes": [{"clause_kind": "outer_select", "original": "COUNT(CASE WHEN location_type = 'Urban' THEN 1 END) - COUNT(CASE WHEN location_type = 'Rural' THEN 1 END)", "replacement": "COUNT(*)", "why_unjustified": "The subtraction of urban-packed minus rural-packed counts is not authorised by any KB entry, column-meaning, or labeled-ambiguity sql_snippet. The user query asked for 'a count of packed houses in our prime locations' \u2014 a single non-negative count, not a difference.", "justified_by": ["primitive"]}, {"clause_kind": "cte", "original": "WITH CrowdedStatus AS (... CASE WHEN <urban-predicate> THEN 'Urban' ELSE 'Rural' END AS location_type ...) ... FROM CrowdedStatus", "replacement": "FROM <joins> WHERE <density-guard> AND <density-gt-2> AND <urban-predicate>", "why_unjustified": "The CTE existed only to feed the unjustified outer subtraction. With the subtraction removed, the CTE collapses into a direct WHERE+JOIN; the urban-predicate moves verbatim from the CASE's WHEN into the WHERE.", "justified_by": ["kb:22", "labeled_ambiguity:prime locations", "knowledge_ambiguity:Urban Household", "primitive"]}], "reasoning_summary": "Removed the unauthorised urban-minus-rural subtraction and collapsed the CTE that existed only to support it. The packed-density predicate is fully sanctioned by labeled_ambiguity 'packed houses' + KB 11 + KB 25; the urban predicate is fully sanctioned by KB 22 + labeled_ambiguity 'prime locations' + knowledge_ambiguity 'Urban Household'. Result: plain COUNT(*) of packed AND prime households, matching the natural reading.", "skill_version": "audit-gold-sql/1.0", "audited_at": "2026-05-14T11:47:11+00:00"}
{"instance_id": "households_10", "selected_database": "households", "audit_status": "unrecoverable", "original_sol_sql": ["WITH TargetHouseholds AS (SELECT h.housenum, h.locregion FROM households h JOIN transportation_assets t ON h.housenum = t.housetag JOIN properties p ON h.housenum = p.houselink JOIN amenities a ON h.housenum = a.houseid WHERE (CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Auto_Count') AS INTEGER) + CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Bike_Count') AS INTEGER) + CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Motor_Count') AS INTEGER)) > 2 AND LOWER(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.Newest_Year')) IN ('2005 to 2009', '2010 to 2013', '2012 to 2013', '2014 or newer') AND LOWER(JSON_EXTRACT(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Dwelling_Class')) IN ('brickwork house', 'apartment') AND LOWER(a.cablestatus) IN ('avail', 'available', 'yes')) SELECT locregion FROM TargetHouseholds GROUP BY locregion ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC LIMIT 1;"], "audited_sol_sql": ["SELECT DISTINCT h.housenum FROM households h JOIN transportation_assets t ON h.housenum = t.housetag JOIN properties p ON h.housenum = p.houselink JOIN amenities a ON h.housenum = a.houseid WHERE (CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Auto_Count') AS INTEGER) + CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Bike_Count') AS INTEGER) + CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Motor_Count') AS INTEGER)) > 2 AND LOWER(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.Newest_Year')) IN ('2005 to 2009', '2010 to 2013', '2012 to 2013', '2014 or newer') AND LOWER(JSON_EXTRACT(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Dwelling_Class')) IN ('brickwork house', 'apartment') AND LOWER(a.cablestatus) IN ('avail', 'available', 'yes');"], "audited_sample_row": [4], "changes": [{"clause_kind": "outer_select", "original": "SELECT locregion FROM TargetHouseholds GROUP BY locregion ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC LIMIT 1", "replacement": "SELECT DISTINCT h.housenum FROM <joins> WHERE <highly-mobile> AND <updated-residence>", "why_unjustified": "User asked for 'home IDs' (housenum list); gold returns the single locregion with the highest TargetHouseholds count. The GROUP-BY-locregion ORDER-BY-COUNT-LIMIT-1 shape contradicts the labeled_ambiguity 'home IDs' = 'h.housenum'.", "justified_by": ["labeled_ambiguity:home IDs", "labeled_ambiguity:highly mobile homes", "labeled_ambiguity:updated residences", "labeled_ambiguity:many vehicles", "knowledge_ambiguity:Mobile Household", "kb:6", "kb:7", "kb:10", "kb:14", "kb:23", "kb:26", "primitive"]}], "reasoning_summary": "Gold projects locregion via a group-by-count-limit-1 instead of the labeled 'home IDs' projection. The per-row filter (mobile + updated-residence + cablestatus) is fully justified by labeled_ambiguity entries and KB 23/26. Audited SQL keeps the predicate verbatim and replaces the outer projection with DISTINCT h.housenum per labeled_ambiguity 'home IDs'.", "skill_version": "audit-gold-sql/1.0", "audited_at": "2026-05-14T11:47:11+00:00"}
{"instance_id": "households_11", "selected_database": "households", "audit_status": "unrecoverable", "original_sol_sql": ["WITH HouseholdScores AS (SELECT h.housenum, i.parkavail, CASE h.socioeconomic ->> 'Income_Bracket' WHEN 'More than R$ 4,400' THEN 6 WHEN 'More than R$ 2,640 and less than R$ 4,400' THEN 5 WHEN 'More than R$ 1,760 and less than R$ 2,640' THEN 4 WHEN 'More than R$ 880 and less than R$ 1,760' THEN 3 WHEN 'More than R$ 880 and less' THEN 2 WHEN 'Has no income' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END AS income_score, CASE UPPER(h.socioeconomic ->> 'Tenure_Type') WHEN 'OWNED' THEN 3 WHEN 'RENTED' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END AS tenure_score, CAST(REPLACE(h.socioeconomic ->> 'Expend_Coeff', ',', '.') AS REAL) AS expend_coeff FROM households h JOIN properties p ON h.housenum = p.houselink JOIN infrastructure i ON p.infralink = i.infraref WHERE h.socioeconomic ->> 'Income_Bracket' IS NOT NULL AND (h.socioeconomic ->> 'Income_Bracket') <> 'Has no income'), SEI_Scores AS (SELECT housenum, parkavail, (0.4 * income_score + 0.4 * (1 - expend_coeff) + 0.2 * tenure_score) AS sei FROM HouseholdScores), Top10 AS (SELECT parkavail FROM SEI_Scores ORDER BY sei DESC LIMIT 10) SELECT ROUND(COALESCE(AVG(CASE WHEN UPPER(parkavail) = 'AVAILABLE' THEN 1.0 ELSE 0.0 END) * 100, 0), 2) FROM Top10;"], "audited_sol_sql": ["WITH HouseholdScores AS (SELECT h.housenum, h.locregion, CASE json_extract(h.socioeconomic, '$.Income_Bracket') WHEN 'More than R$ 4,400' THEN 6 WHEN 'More than R$ 2,640 and less than R$ 4,400' THEN 5 WHEN 'More than R$ 1,760 and less than R$ 2,640' THEN 4 WHEN 'More than R$ 880 and less than R$ 1,760' THEN 3 WHEN 'More than R$ 880 and less' THEN 2 WHEN 'Has no income' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END AS income_score, CASE UPPER(json_extract(h.socioeconomic, '$.Tenure_Type')) WHEN 'OWNED' THEN 3 WHEN 'RENTED' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END AS tenure_score, CAST(REPLACE(json_extract(h.socioeconomic, '$.Expend_Coeff'), ',', '.') AS REAL) AS expend_coeff FROM households h WHERE json_extract(h.socioeconomic, '$.Income_Bracket') IS NOT NULL AND json_extract(h.socioeconomic, '$.Income_Bracket') <> 'Has no income') SELECT housenum, locregion, (0.4 * income_score + 0.4 * (1 - expend_coeff) + 0.2 * tenure_score) AS sei FROM HouseholdScores ORDER BY sei DESC LIMIT 10;"], "audited_sample_row": [6456, "Gama", -7.51712], "changes": [{"clause_kind": "outer_select", "original": "Top10 AS (SELECT parkavail FROM SEI_Scores ORDER BY sei DESC LIMIT 10) SELECT ROUND(COALESCE(AVG(CASE WHEN UPPER(parkavail) = 'AVAILABLE' THEN 1.0 ELSE 0.0 END) * 100, 0), 2) FROM Top10", "replacement": "SELECT housenum, locregion, sei FROM HouseholdScores ORDER BY sei DESC LIMIT 10", "why_unjustified": "User asked for top 10 with ID + area + score; gold returns a single percentage = share of top-10 with 'AVAILABLE' parking. The parking-percentage projection is not in any source. The user query's projection (ID + area + score) is class-3 justified via labeled_ambiguity 'ID', 'area', 'overall financial health'.", "justified_by": ["labeled_ambiguity:ID", "labeled_ambiguity:area", "labeled_ambiguity:overall financial health", "labeled_ambiguity:top 10", "knowledge_ambiguity:Socioeconomic Index", "kb:19", "primitive"]}, {"clause_kind": "literal_threshold", "original": "income_score (1..6 ordinal mapping)", "replacement": "(unchanged - kept verbatim)", "why_unjustified": "The 1-6 ordinal mapping for Income_Bracket is not in any KB entry, column-meaning, or labeled-ambiguity sql_snippet. The labeled ambiguity for 'overall financial health' uses 'income_score' as an undefined variable. Keeping the mapping is the minimum scaffolding required to evaluate the labeled SEI formula. Flagged here so a future audit can resolve.", "justified_by": ["labeled_ambiguity:overall financial health", "kb:19"]}], "reasoning_summary": "Gold's output is wrong (single percentage of parking availability among the top 10) and its income_score mapping is unsanctioned. Audited SQL keeps the labeled SEI formula but changes the output to (housenum, locregion, sei) per the labeled-ambiguity projections, ordered by SEI DESC LIMIT 10. The 1-6 income mapping is preserved as the minimum scaffolding for evaluating SEI; documented as a known unjustified scaffold.", "skill_version": "audit-gold-sql/1.0", "audited_at": "2026-05-14T11:47:11+00:00"}
{"instance_id": "households_12", "selected_database": "households", "audit_status": "unrecoverable", "original_sol_sql": ["WITH IndependentHouseholds AS (SELECT h.housenum, h.residentcount, LOWER(JSON_EXTRACT(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Dwelling_Class')) AS dwelling_class, (COALESCE(CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Auto_Count') AS INTEGER), 0) + COALESCE(CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Bike_Count') AS INTEGER), 0) + COALESCE(CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Motor_Count') AS INTEGER), 0)) AS total_vehicles, CASE LOWER(TRIM(JSON_EXTRACT(h.socioeconomic, '$.Income_Bracket'))) WHEN 'low income' THEN 1 WHEN 'lower middle' THEN 2 WHEN 'middle income' THEN 3 WHEN 'upper middle' THEN 4 WHEN 'high income' THEN 5 WHEN 'very high income' THEN 6 ELSE 0 END AS income_score FROM households h LEFT JOIN service_types s ON h.serviceplan = s.serviceref JOIN transportation_assets t ON h.housenum = t.housetag JOIN properties p ON h.housenum = p.houselink WHERE (s.serviceref IS NULL OR (LOWER(s.domestichelp) = 'no domestic workers' AND s.socsupport = 'No')) AND (COALESCE(CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Auto_Count') AS INTEGER), 0) + COALESCE(CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Bike_Count') AS INTEGER), 0) + COALESCE(CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Motor_Count') AS INTEGER), 0)) > 1), TopDwelling AS (SELECT dwelling_class FROM IndependentHouseholds WHERE income_score > 0 GROUP BY dwelling_class ORDER BY AVG(residentcount * income_score) DESC LIMIT 1) SELECT SUM(total_vehicles) FROM IndependentHouseholds WHERE dwelling_class = (SELECT dwelling_class FROM TopDwelling);"], "audited_sol_sql": ["WITH IndependentHouseholds AS (SELECT h.housenum, h.residentcount, LOWER(JSON_EXTRACT(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Dwelling_Class')) AS dwelling_class, (COALESCE(CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Auto_Count') AS INTEGER), 0) + COALESCE(CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Bike_Count') AS INTEGER), 0) + COALESCE(CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Motor_Count') AS INTEGER), 0)) AS total_vehicles, CASE json_extract(h.socioeconomic, '$.Income_Bracket') WHEN 'More than R$ 4,400' THEN 6 WHEN 'More than R$ 2,640 and less than R$ 4,400' THEN 5 WHEN 'More than R$ 1,760 and less than R$ 2,640' THEN 4 WHEN 'More than R$ 880 and less than R$ 1,760' THEN 3 WHEN 'More than R$ 880 and less' THEN 2 WHEN 'Has no income' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END AS income_score FROM households h LEFT JOIN service_types s ON h.serviceplan = s.serviceref JOIN transportation_assets t ON h.housenum = t.housetag JOIN properties p ON h.housenum = p.houselink WHERE (s.serviceref IS NULL OR (LOWER(s.domestichelp) = 'no domestic workers' AND s.socsupport = 'No')) AND (COALESCE(CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Auto_Count') AS INTEGER), 0) + COALESCE(CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Bike_Count') AS INTEGER), 0) + COALESCE(CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Motor_Count') AS INTEGER), 0)) > 1), TopDwelling AS (SELECT dwelling_class FROM IndependentHouseholds WHERE income_score > 0 GROUP BY dwelling_class ORDER BY AVG(residentcount * income_score) DESC LIMIT 1) SELECT dwelling_class, SUM(total_vehicles) AS total_vehicles FROM IndependentHouseholds WHERE dwelling_class = (SELECT dwelling_class FROM TopDwelling) GROUP BY dwelling_class;"], "audited_sample_row": ["other", 7], "changes": [{"clause_kind": "case_branch", "original": "CASE LOWER(TRIM(json_extract(h.socioeconomic, '$.Income_Bracket'))) WHEN 'low income' THEN 1 WHEN 'lower middle' THEN 2 ... WHEN 'very high income' THEN 6 ELSE 0 END", "replacement": "CASE json_extract(h.socioeconomic, '$.Income_Bracket') WHEN 'More than R$ 4,400' THEN 6 ... WHEN 'Has no income' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END", "why_unjustified": "Gold maps the KB-2-named labels ('low income', 'lower middle', etc.) which DO NOT appear in the data \u2014 the data uses R$-range strings ('More than R$ 4,400', etc.). Result: income_score = 0 for every row, making the prosperity-score ranking trivial. The audited mapping uses the actual R$ values from the data, ordering them by ascending R$ \u2014 still unjustified by source but at least computes meaningfully. Documented as a dataset-data-vs-KB mismatch.", "justified_by": ["column_meaning:households|households|socioeconomic|Income_Bracket"]}, {"clause_kind": "outer_select", "original": "SELECT SUM(total_vehicles) FROM IndependentHouseholds WHERE dwelling_class = (SELECT dwelling_class FROM TopDwelling)", "replacement": "SELECT dwelling_class, SUM(total_vehicles) AS total_vehicles FROM IndependentHouseholds WHERE dwelling_class = (SELECT dwelling_class FROM TopDwelling) GROUP BY dwelling_class", "why_unjustified": "User asked TWO things: 'which dwelling type' and 'how many vehicles'. Gold drops the dwelling_class from the projection (returning a single number). Audited adds dwelling_class to match the user's request.", "justified_by": ["labeled_ambiguity:dwelling type", "primitive"]}], "reasoning_summary": "Gold's income_score CASE references KB-2 labels ('low income' etc.) that don't appear in the actual data (data uses R$ ranges) \u2014 every row gets income_score=0, making the prosperity ranking arbitrary. Gold also drops 'dwelling type' from the output despite the user explicitly asking for it. Audited SQL substitutes the data-aligned R$ mapping (flagged as unjustified-but-data-aligned) and adds dwelling_class to the projection. labeled_ambiguity 'prosperity score' (= residentcount * income_score) is preserved.", "skill_version": "audit-gold-sql/1.0", "audited_at": "2026-05-14T11:47:11+00:00"}
{"instance_id": "households_14", "selected_database": "households", "audit_status": "unrecoverable", "original_sol_sql": ["WITH LivingScores AS (SELECT h.housenum, h.socioeconomic ->> 'Expend_Coeff' AS expend_coeff, (0.5 * (CASE UPPER(p.dwelling_specs ->> 'Dwelling_Class') WHEN 'APARTMENT' THEN 4 WHEN 'BRICKWORK HOUSE' THEN 3 ELSE 1 END) + 0.5 * ((CASE WHEN UPPER(i.wateraccess) = 'MUNICIPAL PIPED' THEN 4 ELSE 1 END + CASE WHEN UPPER(i.roadsurface) IN ('PAVED ASPHALT', 'CONCRETE') THEN 4 ELSE 1 END + CASE WHEN UPPER(i.parkavail) = 'PRIVATE GARAGE' THEN 4 ELSE 1 END) / 3.0)) AS lcs, CAST(REPLACE(p.dwelling_specs ->> 'Bath_Count', ',', '') AS REAL) / NULLIF(h.residentcount, 0) AS bathroom_ratio FROM households h JOIN properties p ON h.housenum = p.houselink JOIN infrastructure i ON p.infralink = i.infraref) SELECT CAST(housenum AS INTEGER) FROM LivingScores WHERE lcs > 2 AND bathroom_ratio > 0.5 AND expend_coeff IS NOT NULL ORDER BY CAST(expend_coeff AS REAL) DESC LIMIT 1;"], "audited_sol_sql": ["WITH LivingScores AS (SELECT h.housenum, (0.5 * (CASE UPPER(p.dwelling_specs ->> 'Dwelling_Class') WHEN 'APARTMENT' THEN 4 WHEN 'BRICKWORK HOUSE' THEN 3 ELSE 1 END) + 0.5 * ((CASE WHEN UPPER(i.wateraccess) = 'MUNICIPAL PIPED' THEN 4 ELSE 1 END + CASE WHEN UPPER(i.roadsurface) IN ('PAVED ASPHALT', 'CONCRETE') THEN 4 ELSE 1 END + CASE WHEN UPPER(i.parkavail) = 'PRIVATE GARAGE' THEN 4 ELSE 1 END) / 3.0)) AS lcs, CAST(REPLACE(p.dwelling_specs ->> 'Bath_Count', ',', '') AS REAL) / NULLIF(h.residentcount, 0) AS bathroom_ratio FROM households h JOIN properties p ON h.housenum = p.houselink JOIN infrastructure i ON p.infralink = i.infraref) SELECT housenum, bathroom_ratio FROM LivingScores WHERE lcs > 2 AND bathroom_ratio > 0.5 ORDER BY bathroom_ratio DESC;"], "audited_sample_row": [5940, 3.0], "changes": [{"clause_kind": "order_by", "original": "ORDER BY CAST(expend_coeff AS REAL) DESC LIMIT 1", "replacement": "ORDER BY bathroom_ratio DESC", "why_unjustified": "User asked to 'sort them by that metric' where 'that metric' = bathroom-to-person; gold sorts by expend_coeff and LIMITs to 1. Neither the ORDER BY expend_coeff nor the LIMIT 1 is justified by any source \u2014 the labeled_ambiguity 'bathroom-to-person metric' explicitly aliases bathroom_ratio.", "justified_by": ["labeled_ambiguity:bathroom-to-person metric", "primitive"]}, {"clause_kind": "projection", "original": "SELECT CAST(housenum AS INTEGER) FROM LivingScores", "replacement": "SELECT housenum, bathroom_ratio FROM LivingScores", "why_unjustified": "User asked to 'show their bathroom-to-person metric' \u2014 the gold projects only housenum, dropping the metric the user wanted to see. Audited adds bathroom_ratio to the projection.", "justified_by": ["labeled_ambiguity:bathroom-to-person metric", "primitive"]}, {"clause_kind": "where_predicate", "original": "AND expend_coeff IS NOT NULL", "replacement": "(removed)", "why_unjustified": "The expend_coeff IS NOT NULL filter was only there because the gold sorted by expend_coeff; with that sort gone, the filter has no purpose.", "justified_by": ["primitive"]}], "reasoning_summary": "Gold sorts by expend_coeff (not mentioned in user query) and LIMITs to 1, while user asked for 'a list' sorted by bathroom-to-person metric. Gold also drops bathroom_ratio from the projection. Audited keeps the labeled 'good quality of life' predicate (lcs > 2 AND bathroom_ratio > 0.5), projects (housenum, bathroom_ratio), and sorts by bathroom_ratio DESC.", "skill_version": "audit-gold-sql/1.0", "audited_at": "2026-05-14T11:47:11+00:00"}
{"instance_id": "households_15", "selected_database": "households", "audit_status": "unrecoverable", "original_sol_sql": ["WITH AtRisk AS (SELECT h.housenum, TRIM(LOWER(h.locregion)) AS locregion FROM households h JOIN service_types s ON h.serviceplan = s.serviceref JOIN properties p ON h.housenum = p.houselink WHERE s.socsupport = 'Yes' AND CAST(REPLACE(JSON_EXTRACT(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Room_Count'), '\"', '') AS REAL) > 0 AND (h.residentcount / CAST(REPLACE(JSON_EXTRACT(p.dwelling_specs, '$.Room_Count'), '\"', '') AS REAL)) > 4), RegionalCounts AS (SELECT locregion, COUNT(*) AS at_risk_count FROM AtRisk GROUP BY locregion), TotalCounts AS (SELECT TRIM(LOWER(locregion)) AS locregion, COUNT(*) AS total_count FROM households GROUP BY TRIM(LOWER(locregion))) SELECT rc.locregion FROM RegionalCounts rc JOIN TotalCounts tc ON rc.locregion = tc.locregion ORDER BY (CAST(rc.at_risk_count AS REAL) / tc.total_count) DESC LIMIT 1;"], "audited_sol_sql": ["WITH HouseholdScores AS (SELECT h.housenum, s.domestichelp, s.socsupport, CASE json_extract(h.socioeconomic, '$.Income_Bracket') WHEN 'More than R$ 4,400' THEN 6 WHEN 'More than R$ 2,640 and less than R$ 4,400' THEN 5 WHEN 'More than R$ 1,760 and less than R$ 2,640' THEN 4 WHEN 'More than R$ 880 and less than R$ 1,760' THEN 3 WHEN 'More than R$ 880 and less' THEN 2 WHEN 'Has no income' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END AS income_score, CASE UPPER(json_extract(h.socioeconomic, '$.Tenure_Type')) WHEN 'OWNED' THEN 3 WHEN 'RENTED' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END AS tenure_score, CAST(REPLACE(json_extract(h.socioeconomic, '$.Expend_Coeff'), ',', '.') AS REAL) AS expend_coeff FROM households h LEFT JOIN service_types s ON h.serviceplan = s.serviceref) SELECT DISTINCT housenum FROM HouseholdScores WHERE ((CASE WHEN LOWER(COALESCE(domestichelp,'')) = 'none' THEN 0 ELSE 3 END) + (CASE WHEN COALESCE(socsupport,'') = 'No' THEN 0 ELSE 4 END)) > 2 AND income_score > 0 AND (0.4 * income_score + 0.4 * (expend_coeff / NULLIF(income_score * 1.0, 0)) + 0.2 * tenure_score) > 0.7 AND (expend_coeff / NULLIF(income_score * 1.0, 0)) < 1.5;"], "audited_sample_row": [], "changes": [{"clause_kind": "outer_select", "original": "WITH AtRisk AS (... WHERE s.socsupport = 'Yes' AND density > 4) ... SELECT rc.locregion FROM RegionalCounts rc JOIN TotalCounts tc ON ... ORDER BY (at_risk_count/total_count) DESC LIMIT 1", "replacement": "SELECT DISTINCT housenum FROM HouseholdScores WHERE <highly-supported> AND <financially-secure>", "why_unjustified": "Gold filters by socsupport='Yes' AND density>4 (the 'AtRisk' name suggests it's auditing 'at-risk overcrowded' households \u2014 but the user query is about 'highly supported AND financially secure'). The density>4 threshold and the 'AtRisk' bucketing are not in any source. Gold returns a single locregion via highest-ratio sort, while user asked for 'unique house codes' (DISTINCT housenum). Audited SQL replaces the predicate with the labeled_ambiguity sql_snippets for 'highly supported homes' AND 'financially secure', and projects DISTINCT housenum.", "justified_by": ["labeled_ambiguity:highly supported homes", "labeled_ambiguity:financially secure", "labeled_ambiguity:unique house codes", "knowledge_ambiguity:Well-Equipped Household", "kb:9", "kb:11", "kb:24", "kb:25", "primitive"]}, {"clause_kind": "literal_threshold", "original": "income_score (1..6 ordinal mapping)", "replacement": "(unchanged - kept as scaffolding)", "why_unjustified": "Same caveat as households_11/12: the 1-6 income mapping is not in any source but is required scaffolding for the labeled SEI formula referenced by labeled_ambiguity 'financially secure'.", "justified_by": ["labeled_ambiguity:financially secure", "kb:11"]}], "reasoning_summary": "Gold's predicate uses an unjustified density>4 'AtRisk' bucketing and ignores the labeled 'highly supported' + 'financially secure' definitions entirely; output is wrong (returns one locregion, user asked for DISTINCT housenum). Audited SQL uses the two labeled-ambiguity sql_snippets verbatim and projects DISTINCT housenum. Notes: (a) labeled 'financially secure' references income_score/tenure_score variables; we use the same 1-6 income mapping as in households_11 as scaffolding, (b) actual result is 0 rows because few households simultaneously match both predicates given the dataset's value distribution.", "skill_version": "audit-gold-sql/1.0", "audited_at": "2026-05-14T11:47:11+00:00"}
{"instance_id": "households_16", "selected_database": "households", "audit_status": "clean", "original_sol_sql": ["SELECT json_extract(socioeconomic, '$.Income_Bracket') AS income_classification FROM households WHERE housenum = 3;"], "audited_sol_sql": ["SELECT json_extract(socioeconomic, '$.Income_Bracket') AS income_classification FROM households WHERE housenum = 3;"], "audited_sample_row": ["More than R$ 4,400 and less than R$ 8,800"], "changes": [], "reasoning_summary": "Trivial query. 'economic status' = Income_Bracket extraction (labeled + knowledge_ambiguity 'Income Classification' deleted_kb=2 + KB 2). 'house' = FROM households (labeled). 'ID 3' = WHERE housenum=3 (labeled). All clauses class-3 + KB justified.", "skill_version": "audit-gold-sql/1.0", "audited_at": "2026-05-14T11:47:11+00:00"}
{"instance_id": "households_17", "selected_database": "households", "audit_status": "clean", "original_sol_sql": ["SELECT COUNT(*) FROM households WHERE TRIM(LOWER(locregion)) = 'taguatinga' AND LOWER(json_extract(socioeconomic, '$.Tenure_Type')) = 'owned' AND LOWER(json_extract(socioeconomic, '$.Income_Bracket')) IN ('high income', 'very high income');"], "audited_sol_sql": ["SELECT COUNT(*) FROM households WHERE TRIM(LOWER(locregion)) = 'taguatinga' AND LOWER(json_extract(socioeconomic, '$.Tenure_Type')) = 'owned' AND LOWER(json_extract(socioeconomic, '$.Income_Bracket')) IN ('high income', 'very high income');"], "audited_sample_row": [0], "changes": [], "reasoning_summary": "Every clause is class-3 + KB justified. 'residences' = FROM households (labeled). 'wealthy' = Tenure='OWNED' AND Income_Bracket IN ('high income','very high income') (labeled + knowledge_ambiguity 'Affluent Household' + KB 21). 'Taguatinga area' = TRIM(LOWER(locregion))='taguatinga' (labeled). Note: this query returns 0 against the actual data because the data's Income_Bracket values are R$ ranges (e.g. 'More than R$ 4,400'), not the labeled categorical names. This is a dataset data-vs-label mismatch, not an audit issue \u2014 the gold faithfully reflects the labels.", "skill_version": "audit-gold-sql/1.0", "audited_at": "2026-05-14T11:47:11+00:00"}
{"instance_id": "households_19", "selected_database": "households", "audit_status": "clean", "original_sol_sql": ["WITH UrbanHouseholds AS (SELECT h.housenum FROM households h JOIN properties p ON h.housenum = p.houselink JOIN infrastructure i ON p.infralink = i.infraref WHERE LOWER(i.wateraccess) LIKE 'yes,%' AND LOWER(i.roadsurface) = 'asphalt, concrete') SELECT t.housetag FROM transportation_assets t JOIN UrbanHouseholds u ON t.housetag = u.housenum ORDER BY CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Auto_Count') AS INTEGER) DESC LIMIT 1;"], "audited_sol_sql": ["WITH UrbanHouseholds AS (SELECT h.housenum FROM households h JOIN properties p ON h.housenum = p.houselink JOIN infrastructure i ON p.infralink = i.infraref WHERE LOWER(i.wateraccess) LIKE 'yes,%' AND LOWER(i.roadsurface) = 'asphalt, concrete') SELECT t.housetag FROM transportation_assets t JOIN UrbanHouseholds u ON t.housetag = u.housenum ORDER BY CAST(JSON_EXTRACT(t.vehicleinventory, '$.vehicle_counts.Auto_Count') AS INTEGER) DESC LIMIT 1;"], "audited_sample_row": [1670], "changes": [], "reasoning_summary": "Every clause is class-3 + KB justified. 'home ID' = t.housetag (labeled). 'highest car count' = ORDER BY Auto_Count DESC LIMIT 1 (labeled). 'urban homes' is operationalised via LOWER+LIKE/equality on wateraccess and roadsurface \u2014 this differs literally from the labeled-ambiguity sql_snippet (which uses 'Municipal Piped'/'Paved Asphalt') but is justified at concept-level by KB 3 (Water Access: 'Yes' = piped) + KB 4 (Road Surface: 'Asphalt'/'Concrete' = high quality) + KB 22 (Urban Household = piped + paved). knowledge_ambiguity 'Urban Household' (deleted_kb=22) corroborates. Note: the gold's strict-equality LIKE/= on roadsurface may miss whitespace variants in the data, but that's an operational quirk, not an audit issue.", "skill_version": "audit-gold-sql/1.0", "audited_at": "2026-05-14T11:47:11+00:00"}
